      "utf8": "bureaucracy of the Fed itself. Powell is of course \nthe chairman of the Federal Reserve. But to get  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 355040,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that role he is first also a sitting governor of \nits board. The chairman is appointed to four years  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 360400,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at a time and this is the role where Powell's term \nis about to be up. A Fed governor is appointed to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 366000,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "14 years and once they are in that seat, they are \nextraordinarily difficult to remove by design.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 371280,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Both to keep the Fed independent from political \npressure and to stop governors from bowing to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 375520,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "whoever happens to be in the White House in that \ndecade. And it is actually the governorship,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 380400,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "not the chairmanship, that carries most of \nthe real power. Each governor gets a vote on  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 385120,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the Federal Open Market Committee, which is the \ncommittee that actually sets interest rates. This  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 389360,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "committee is made up of seven governors from the \nFed in Washington, of which one is the chairman,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 394000,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as well as representatives from five out of the \n12 regional Federal Reserve branches to make a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 398640,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "total of 12 voting parties. Out of this group, \nthe chairman is more of a first amongst equals  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 404000,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "kind of role responsible for communicating \nwhat the Fed is doing, running the meetings,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 408080,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and managing the institution's public face \nthrough press conferences. But the actual  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 412000,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "decisions on rates themselves are made by a \nvote between everybody on the committee with  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 416480,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "everybody getting an equal vote. Now, this is a \nproblem for an administration that wants to use  "
    } ]
