    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by the other 11 people in the room, which creates \nan even bigger problem for the administration.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 431040,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because while Powell's term as chairman is up in a \nweek, his term as governor doesn't end until 2028.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 437120,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This bureaucratic detail is important because if \nPowell refuses to give up his seat as governor,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 441600,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the Fed doesn't just make another one. There are \nexactly seven seats on the board of governors.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 447440,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They are set by statute. So if Worsh wants \nto be chairman of the board of governors,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 451680,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he needs to be a governor first. If he doesn't \nhave a seat, he can't be the chairman regardless  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 456480,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of what the Senate eventually decides. Now, the \nonly bit of good news for the administration is  "
    } ]
