    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of his official term, which ended back in January. \nSo, if Powell absolutely refuses to budge, Wars  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 471440,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "could theoretically just take Myron's spot. But \nthat also means the White House loses one of its  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 477120,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "own friendly appointees on the board, who is more \nlikely to vote on rate cuts, which sort of defeats  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 482000,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the whole point of this exercise. What they really \nwant is for Powell to bow out gracefully, which  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 487040,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "would then let them reappoint Myron to a brand \nnew 14-year term and slot war into Powell's old  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 492320,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "seat to get a much bigger friendly voting block \nestablishment on the committee. Now, typically,  "
    } ]
